asr-000279
00:18:54.140 --> 00:19:10.200
GCG Chairperson Atty. Marius P. Corpus: With total obligations reaching P218.322 million, our net budget utilization rate steps up to 56.10% as we head into the final third of the fiscal year.

asr-000280
00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:23.700
GCG Chairperson Atty. Marius P. Corpus: This multi-year trend highlights the GECG's budget trajectory, anchored by two major funding spikes directly tied to the compensation and position classification system.

asr-000281
00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:45.920
GCG Chairperson Atty. Marius P. Corpus: The first spike in 2019, funding rose sharply to $258.2 million for the initial implementation, maintaining a strong 80% utilization rate.

asr-000282
00:19:45.920 --> 00:19:53.900
GCG Chairperson Atty. Marius P. Corpus: The second spike in 2023 for the second review, allocation peaked at an all-time high of P421.6 million.

asr-000284
00:19:54.140 --> 00:20:24.120
GCG Chairperson Atty. Marius P. Corpus: This comprehensive review tested our absorption capacity. The true success story follows those spikes. [laughter] As funding normalized in 2024 and 2025, we achieved operational efficiency, driving our budget utilization rates up to 88.93% and 90.59%.

asr-000287
00:20:24.420 --> 00:20:38.640
GCG Chairperson Atty. Marius P. Corpus: Currently, for 2026, we stand at $394.5 million, with utilization tracking steadily at 51.56% as of mid-year.

asr-000288
00:20:39.860 --> 00:20:51.940
GCG Chairperson Atty. Marius P. Corpus: Moving into 2027, the proposed $408.3 million NEP ceiling ensures we sustain this momentum and continue our rigorous oversight mandates.

